# pnpm's default `verify-deps-before-run=install` re-runs `pnpm install`
# before every `pnpm run`/`pnpm test`/etc, and that re-run is broken for a
# workspace member as of pnpm 11.24: run from inside apps/playground or
# packages/ui, it reports ERR_PNPM_WORKSPACE_PKG_NOT_FOUND, seeing zero
# packages in the workspace, even though `pnpm install` at the repo root
# works fine and the member's own `.npmrc` inheritance does NOT rescue it -
# this setting is turned off here only as a safety net for a developer
# running `cd apps/playground && pnpm run ...` by habit.
#
# THE REAL FIX IS CWD, NOT THIS FILE - `--filter` only dodges the bug when
# pnpm's own cwd is the repo root; run `pnpm --filter playground run build`
# FROM apps/playground and it fails exactly the same way. Every committed
# invocation either runs `pnpm --filter <name> run <script>` from the repo
# root (Makefile, CI) or, where the surrounding script already lives inside
# a workspace member (scripts/dusk.sh), sets
# `PNPM_CONFIG_VERIFY_DEPS_BEFORE_RUN=false` on that one command instead.
# `pnpm install` already runs explicitly wherever it's needed, so the
# automatic re-check has nothing to add either way.
verify-deps-before-run=false
